WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.460
Hello.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:10.230
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.610
In this sixth episode, we'll look at the
kinds of medicine used for mood disorders,

4
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:22.650
their common side effects, and a few rare but
important warning signs that are good to know.

5
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:29.120
Just as diabetes is treated with medicine,
diet, exercise and family support,

6
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.240
a mood disorder needs medication
together with a regular daily routine,

7
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.720
stress management and the support of your family.

8
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:42.320
Beyond a certain point, symptoms can't
be controlled by willpower alone.

9
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:49.670
The goal of treatment goes beyond the acute symptoms:
to prevent relapse and get your daily life back.

10
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:58.060
Mood disorders, and bipolar disorder in
particular, come from changes in brain function,

11
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.360
so medication is at the centre of treatment.

12
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.120
First, mood stabilisers.

13
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:11.520
Mood stabilisers calm the over-excitement of
nerve cells and reduce the big swings in mood.

14
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:18.060
They are used to settle mania and prevent
relapse, and some also help with depression.

15
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.500
The best-known one is lithium.

16
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.780
It has the longest track record and the best-established

17
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.880
evidence for treating mania and preventing relapse,

18
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.720
and some studies suggest it may
help lower the risk of suicide.

19
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.973
Valproate (Depakote),

20
00:01:34.993 --> 00:01:41.770
carbamazepine and lamotrigine (Lamictal)
were first developed to treat epilepsy,

21
00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.195
and were later found to stabilise mood as well.

22
00:01:45.215 --> 00:01:50.068
That is why they are also called anticonvulsants.

23
00:01:50.088 --> 00:01:55.920
Oxcarbazepine, a medicine similar to
carbamazepine, is sometimes used too.

24
00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.360
Each medicine works best for
slightly different symptoms.

25
00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.960
Valproate and carbamazepine are used mainly for mania.

26
00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.420
Lamotrigine is not a treatment for mania,

27
00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:13.570
but it is used for bipolar depression and to
prevent depressive episodes from coming back.

28
00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:19.259
Valproate can raise the risk of birth defects
and developmental problems in the baby,

29
00:02:19.279 --> 00:02:24.420
so for anyone who could become pregnant,
other medicines are considered first.

30
00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.989
If it is really needed,

31
00:02:26.009 --> 00:02:30.079
talk with your doctor in advance about
contraception and pregnancy plans.

32
00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:32.102
And if you find out you are pregnant,

33
00:02:32.122 --> 00:02:36.210
don't stop it on your own;
contact your doctor straight away.

34
00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.280
Next, antipsychotics.

35
00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.200
These medicines mainly act on
the dopamine receptors in the

36
00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.260
brain and turn down dopamine
signals that have become overactive.

37
00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.140
Depending on the medicine, they also act
on receptors for other brain chemicals,

38
00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.390
such as serotonin.

39
00:02:54.610 --> 00:03:00.190
They were named antipsychotics because
they help so much with psychotic symptoms,

40
00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.780
but they are not used only for psychosis.

41
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.260
They work well for mania, and some are
proven to help with bipolar depression too.

42
00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.660
They are also used to help with sleep,

43
00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:17.560
or to reduce symptoms such as
delusions or hearing voices.

44
00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:25.450
Antidepressants boost the action of neurotransmitters
such as serotonin to lift a depressed mood,

45
00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.710
and they can also help with eating and sleeping.

46
00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.466
In bipolar depression, however,

47
00:03:31.486 --> 00:03:36.437
antidepressants are used carefully
and only for those who need them,

48
00:03:36.457 --> 00:03:40.962
and in bipolar type I disorder
they are not used on their own.

49
00:03:40.982 --> 00:03:44.259
This is because the mood can swing towards mania.

50
00:03:44.279 --> 00:03:51.317
If you feel unusually elated or excited, or are
sleeping less, tell your doctor straight away.

51
00:03:51.337 --> 00:03:54.040
Your doctor can adjust your treatment.

52
00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:59.660
Tranquillisers control anxiety
and insomnia in the acute phase.

53
00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.680
They help when symptoms are severe,

54
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.340
but with long use they can lose
their effect or lead to dependence,

55
00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.890
so it is best to use them only
for as long as you really need.

56
00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.970
If you keep needing a lot of tranquillisers,

57
00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:21.070
it may be a sign that your main treatment needs
further adjusting, so talk with your doctor.

58
00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:21.590
Also,

59
00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:27.650
stopping a tranquilliser suddenly after taking it
for a long time can cause withdrawal symptoms.

60
00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:32.150
Don't stop it on your own; taper it
slowly together with your doctor.

61
00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.840
Just as cold medicines and digestive
medicines can have side effects,

62
00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.970
medicines for mood disorders can too.

63
00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:46.150
Each medicine has its own suitable
length of use and its own precautions.

64
00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.610
Taking the medicines you need properly,

65
00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:54.510
monitoring your symptoms and keeping up with
regular tests helps lower the risk of side effects.

66
00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:59.050
Knowing about the important ones in
advance, even if they are uncommon,

67
00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.970
can help you respond calmly if one appears.

68
00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:08.710
Many side effects improve when the medicine is
adjusted, but a few signs need prompt action,

69
00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.090
so let's go through them together.

70
00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:17.700
Akathisia is an inner restlessness:
you can't sit or stand still,

71
00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:22.170
and you may rock your body or keep
sitting down and standing up.

72
00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:28.430
It can happen with antipsychotics, and
some antidepressants can cause it too.

73
00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:32.050
Because it looks like the agitation of a mood disorder,

74
00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.930
your doctor needs to assess it carefully.

75
00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:39.410
It is managed by lowering or changing
the medicine and, if needed,

76
00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:42.580
adding a medicine such as propranolol.

77
00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:49.120
Acute dystonia is a rare side effect in which the
eyes roll upwards, or the muscles of the neck,

78
00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.700
jaw or tongue suddenly stiffen and twist.

79
00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:57.640
It can be frightening, but it eases
quickly with an injection or a tablet,

80
00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:00.320
so see a doctor right away if it happens.

81
00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.880
If you have trouble breathing or swallowing,

82
00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:06.760
it is safest to get help at the
emergency room straight away.

83
00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:14.260
Hand tremor is fairly common with lithium and
valproate, and antipsychotics can cause it too.

84
00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:20.160
It often improves once the acute phase
has passed and the dose is adjusted,

85
00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:24.780
and a medicine such as propranolol can also help.

86
00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:29.420
But if your tremor suddenly
gets worse, tell your doctor,

87
00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:33.530
as it may be a sign to check your lithium level.

88
00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:41.140
Some antipsychotics raise prolactin,
the hormone that produces breast milk.

89
00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:47.320
Periods may become lighter or stop, milk may
be produced, and sexual function may decline.

90
00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.820
This is called hyperprolactinaemia.

91
00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:56.980
If you notice these changes, don't wait for
your mood to improve first; tell your doctor.

92
00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.440
In most cases they can be managed by lowering the dose,

93
00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:05.150
or by switching to or adding a medicine
with less of this side effect.

94
00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:10.830
Weight can go up, and blood
sugar and cholesterol can rise.

95
00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:16.650
Combine a sensible diet with exercise, have
your weight and blood tests checked regularly,

96
00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:18.230
and if something is off,

97
00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.170
your doctor will weigh the
benefits against the side effects

98
00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:25.250
and adjust the medicine or add the treatment you need.

99
00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:30.270
One caution: appetite suppressants
can affect mood symptoms,

100
00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:33.670
so talk with your doctor before taking one.

101
00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:41.617
Constipation is common, but it is
important to deal with it early.

102
00:07:41.637 --> 00:07:47.578
Antipsychotics, especially clozapine
(Clozaril), can slow the bowel down,

103
00:07:47.598 --> 00:07:56.680
and if constipation is left untreated it can,
rarely, lead to a blocked or paralysed bowel.

104
00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:04.060
High-fibre foods, plenty of water, regular
exercise and a regular toilet routine all help.

105
00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:08.720
If you take clozapine and become
constipated or go less often,

106
00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:11.760
don't wait; tell your doctor straight away.

107
00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:19.340
Starting a laxative early, as your care team
advises, usually keeps it well under control.

108
00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:26.240
Rarely, severe stomach pain, a swollen belly,
vomiting, or not passing wind may appear.

109
00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:31.840
If even one of these happens, it needs to be
checked right away in case the bowel is blocked.

110
00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:37.920
Don't take more laxatives on your own; go to the
emergency room and get examined straight away.

111
00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:46.710
Medicines such as lamotrigine, carbamazepine
and oxcarbazepine, and rarely valproate,

112
00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:48.930
can cause a rash of red spots.

113
00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:53.770
It usually appears within a few weeks of
starting the medicine or raising the dose,

114
00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:57.370
but it can also appear after a long time.

115
00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:00.030
Mild rashes are more common,

116
00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:05.210
but at first they can be hard to tell
apart from a serious skin reaction.

117
00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:11.910
Very rarely, a rash can progress to a serious
skin reaction, so checking early is important.

118
00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:15.570
If a new rash appears while
you are taking these medicines,

119
00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.970
don't take any more of that medicine,

120
00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:22.590
and contact the doctor who prescribed
it straight away to have it checked.

121
00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:25.890
If you can, take a photo of the rash; it helps.

122
00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:31.310
If you have a fever, pain in the mouth
or eyes, blisters, or peeling skin,

123
00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:35.990
it is safest to go to the emergency
room and get examined right away.

124
00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:40.913
Valproate can make hair thinner or cause hair loss,

125
00:09:40.933 --> 00:09:45.256
and lithium can make acne or psoriasis worse.

126
00:09:45.276 --> 00:09:49.206
Acne can be treated with help from a dermatologist,

127
00:09:49.226 --> 00:09:53.899
and hair loss often recovers
once the medicine is adjusted.

128
00:09:53.919 --> 00:09:56.298
Other causes are checked as well.

129
00:09:56.318 --> 00:10:01.805
The benefit of supplements such as biotin
or zinc for this hair loss is uncertain,

130
00:10:01.825 --> 00:10:07.058
so talk with your doctor first if you
want to take them, and if you already do,

131
00:10:07.078 --> 00:10:10.414
tell your doctor before any tests.

132
00:10:10.434 --> 00:10:14.890
Biotin in particular can affect some blood test results.

133
00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:19.990
After taking a sleeping pill such
as zolpidem, or a tranquilliser,

134
00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:25.750
some people act while not fully awake
and have no memory of it afterwards.

135
00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.770
This is called sleep-related behaviour.

136
00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.330
Some get up and eat, or make odd phone calls,

137
00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:38.190
and in rare cases people have driven
a car or fallen and been badly hurt.

138
00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:40.270
If this has happened to you,

139
00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:46.170
stop that sleeping pill and tell the
doctor who prescribed it straight away.

140
00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.550
For sleeping pills such as zolpidem,

141
00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:54.030
the rule is to switch to another approach
rather than use that medicine again.

142
00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:59.450
A tranquilliser taken for a long time
is not stopped suddenly; instead,

143
00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:03.410
you and your care team work out a safe way to taper it.

144
00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:10.190
Take sleeping pills at the lowest dose, only
right before going to bed, and never with alcohol.

145
00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:15.350
Keep them out of reach of children,
and don't share them with anyone.

146
00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:22.083
Also, even without symptoms, blood tests
such as liver, kidney and thyroid function,

147
00:11:22.103 --> 00:11:27.440
blood cell counts, blood sugar and
cholesterol, or an ECG, can show changes.

148
00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:33.000
Regular tests, as your doctor recommends,
let these be found and managed early.

149
00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:39.050
With lithium and valproate, the blood
level of the medicine is checked as well.

150
00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:43.390
If you take lithium, please remember one more thing.

151
00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:49.710
Rarely, severe diarrhoea or vomiting, a
tremor much worse than before, unsteadiness,

152
00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:54.730
slurred speech or feeling dazed can be signs
that your lithium level has become too high.

153
00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:57.310
If this happens, don't take any more lithium,

154
00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:00.350
and go to the emergency room
for assessment straight away.

155
00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.740
Your care team will decide when to restart it.

156
00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:10.660
Your lithium level can rise more easily
when you sweat a lot or become dehydrated,

157
00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:16.900
or when you take anti-inflammatory painkillers
or diuretics, also called water tablets,

158
00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.540
together with lithium.

159
00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:24.090
So drink plenty of water, and tell your
doctor before taking any other medicine.

160
00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:28.300
Each kind of medicine has its own role,

161
00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:33.640
and side effects can often be managed
by lowering or changing the medicine.

162
00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:39.800
As a rule, rather than cutting down or
stopping on your own, talk with your doctor.

163
00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.940
But in the few situations we
covered today, such as a new rash,

164
00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:49.800
signs of possible lithium toxicity, or
sleep-related behaviour after a sleeping pill,

165
00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:53.960
stop that medicine as advised and
contact your care team right away.

166
00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:59.190
Knowing this in advance lets you
respond calmly, without panic.

167
00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:03.070
Next time, we'll talk about how
to take your medicines properly,

168
00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:06.910
and about common misunderstandings about medication.

169
00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:07.950
Thank you.
